{"type":"message","id":"3174fa98","parentId":"1576ec22","timestamp":"2026-10-20T04:09:16.821Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`sort_a` is faster: about 0.17 s against 0.41 s for `sort_b`, roughly 2.5× faster. I wrote `faster: sort_a` to `RESULT.md`.\n\nI timed both on the same 100,000 random ints (seeded, values from 0 to 10⁹), took the best of 3 runs each, and checked both outputs matched `sorted()`.\n\nWhy: `sort_b` calls `bisect.insort` once per element. Each insert can shift up to the whole list, so the total work grows with the square of the input size. The shifting is fast C code, which is why the gap is only about 2.5× at this size. It will get much wider on bigger inputs. `sort_a` is a standard merge sort and scales normally."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"vertex-anthropic","model":"claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":242,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":37629,"totalTokens":37873,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0},"cttl":{"ephemeral5m":37629}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1792469353525,"responseId":"msg_vrtx_011CgCqFr3tVm3nX36E7Ktrm","duration":3295.151501999999,"ttft":3255.788231999999,"contextSnapshot":{"promptTokens":37631,"nonMessageTokens":18444}}}
